    "body": "Rework for the review at `bd69a2177`. The new head is `498ba08b5`.\n\nFinding 1 (a shallow cut into an added part posts):\n- `posting_sim::judge_clause` now runs `kept_moved` in the clean-sim arm when every op is covered (`uncovered` is `None`). This is the proposal of the issue.\n- New pin: `a_part_added_a_hair_under_a_judged_stock_source_chamfer_is_refused_by_name`. It adds a part 0.05 mm into the cut, on aligned and quarter-turned stock. It asserts that the post never goes out, and that the refusal names `S1`, the part `other` and the cause.\n- Mutation check: with the clean-arm change removed, this test fails because the program posts.\n- The two first tests are unchanged and green.\n\nFinding 2 (the Deburr text):\n- The decision now says that a Deburr can take the stock as source, and that the stock-source Deburr gouge is #2313, not fixed here.\n- The \"Dropped\" text now records that the issue's proposal is applied, and why change 1 alone was not sufficient.\n\nSuites: all 15 named suites are green on `498ba08b5`, and clippy `-D warnings` is clean. The PR body has the table.\n",
